  "result": "The rule for NRS_484B_227_1_o1 passed the gate with **OK** on the first run (1 of 6 used). All 6 witness scenarios gave their expected verdicts, and nothing needed fixing.\n\n**What the rule says:**\n- **Who it applies to (s1):** any member of the vehicle group defined in NRS 484A.320.\n- **When it applies (s2):** the vehicle occupies a highway that has a median or divider on it.\n- **The duty (s3):** for every such highway, on every roadway of it the vehicle occupies, the vehicle must not point against that roadway's designated direction. The same check runs separately for every lane of it the vehicle occupies. The duty repeats the full \"divided highway the vehicle is on\" condition rather than relying on a shared variable name.\n- I added no readings of my own, so the narrowings list is empty: the node already spelled out the duty in full, and its own narrowings cover \"driven\" and \"right-hand roadway\".\n\n**Test scenarios** (one divided highway with a median, an eastbound roadway on the right and a westbound one on the left):\n\n| Scenario | Situation | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | car heads east on the westbound roadway | violated |\n| permit | car heads east on the eastbound roadway | compliant |\n| idle | car in the opposing lane of a highway with no median | not applicable |\n| blind | as forbid, with the heading masked | unknown |\n| branch_1 | car turns left at an intersection, crossing the westbound roadway heading north (at right angles to it) | compliant |\n| branch_2 (added) | the westbound roadway has no direction but its lanes do; the car heads against its lane | violated |\n\nI added `branch_2` so the lane check decides a verdict on its own, separately from the roadway check.\n\nFiles are in `library/` and the working directory:\n- `TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_227_1_o1.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_227_1_o1.lean`\n- `task_result.md`",
